IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 22 (ENFORCEMENT OF JUDGMENTS AND ORDERS), rules 6 to 9: how an enforcement order is carried out, sale and
-- valuation of seized property, delivery and giving of possession, the Sheriff's statement of accounts and commission.
-- Rules 1 to 5 are in roc5-o22-order.l4 and rules 10 to 13 in roc5-o22-objection.l4.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc5-o20.l4.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are the text's own yes and no;
-- NOTHING is "not covered"; a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Two rules here are also written as regulative rules (PARTY ... MUST ... WITHIN ... LEST BREACH): rule 6(9)(a) and
-- rule 6(10).  A regulative rule counts a plain number of days from the moment the trace starts; the decision
-- function beside it counts the period by Order 3 rule 3 (an input) and is the one the layer 2 questions use.
-- Seam S-L2: nothing here asks whether the Government is a party (Order 59 rule 11 switches Order 22 off for the
-- Government, in another part).  "Subject to any written law" is not threaded as an input (NOTES.md).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 22, rules 6 to 9 -- the Sheriff`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 6 -- how an enforcement order is carried out`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) and (2): the sequence.
-- src:3450 | 6. —(1) The Sheriff must carry out the terms of the enforcement order in the sequence indicated (if any) in the enforcement order and at the time, place and in the manner determined by the Sheriff, and may exercise any powers under any written law relating to forced entry into premises. (2) If no sequence of enforcement is indicated in the enforcement order, the Sheriff may carry out its terms in any order and sequentially or concurrently, in the Sheriff’s discretion.
@ref O 22 r 6(1) (src:3450-3450)
GIVEN `the enforcement order indicates a sequence of enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 6(1) the Sheriff must carry out the terms of the enforcement order in the sequence indicated` MEANS
    IF `the enforcement order indicates a sequence of enforcement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the sequence indicated (if any) in the enforcement order"

-- src:3450 | 6. —(1) The Sheriff must carry out the terms of the enforcement order in the sequence indicated (if any) in the enforcement order and at the time, place and in the manner determined by the Sheriff, and may exercise any powers under any written law relating to forced entry into premises. (2) If no sequence of enforcement is indicated in the enforcement order, the Sheriff may carry out its terms in any order and sequentially or concurrently, in the Sheriff’s discretion.
@ref O 22 r 6(1) (src:3450-3450)
GIVEN `the Sheriff is carrying out the terms of the enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 6(1) the Sheriff determines the time, place and manner of carrying out the enforcement order` MEANS
