GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 6(6) the copy of the notice is served on the enforcement respondent in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a seizure or attachment has been effected under paragraph (4)`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a seizure or attachment has been effected under paragraph (4)" [when counts as where: delegated-definitions ruling (c) of 2026-11-05]
        IF `the Court has otherwise directed in the enforcement order`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the Court otherwise directs in the enforcement order" and the direction's terms are not in the Rules
        IF `the date the copy of the notice is served on the enforcement respondent` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 7 days after effecting the seizure or attachment" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

DECLARE `o 22 r 6(7) method of service` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 6(7) leaving the copy at the address of the place from which the property was seized`
    `o 22 r 6(7) sending the copy by post to the address of the place from which the property was seized`
    `o 22 r 6(7) another method`

-- (7): "In addition to the methods of service set out in Order 7, Rules 2 and 3" (a seam: Order 7 is another part's).
-- src:3474 | (7) In addition to the methods of service set out in Order 7, Rules 2 and 3, the copy of the notice of seizure or attachment may be served on the enforcement respondent by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the address of the place from which the property was seized.
@ref O 22 r 6(7) (src:3474-3474)
GIVEN method IS A `o 22 r 6(7) method of service`
      `o 7 r 2 the method is a method of service set out in Order 7, Rules 2 and 3` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 6(7) the copy of the notice may be served on the enforcement respondent by the method` MEANS
    CONSIDER method
    WHEN `o 22 r 6(7) leaving the copy at the address of the place from which the property was seized` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 6(7) sending the copy by post to the address of the place from which the property was seized` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 6(7) another method` THEN
        IF `o 7 r 2 the method is a method of service set out in Order 7, Rules 2 and 3` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "In addition to the methods of service set out in Order 7, Rules 2 and 3" and what those rules allow is theirs to say

