-- The same duty as a regulative rule.  Days are counted from the service of the notice (day 0 of the trace).
DECLARE `o 22 r 6 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment`
    `o 22 r 6 the Sheriff`
    `o 22 r 6 the enforcement applicant`

DECLARE `o 22 r 6 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 6(9)(a) informs the Sheriff of the amount owing to the enforcement respondent that is available to be attached`
    `o 22 r 6(10)(a) hands or pays over to the enforcement applicant the money due to the enforcement respondent`
    `o 22 r 6(10)(b) hands or pays over to the Sheriff the commission due to the Sheriff`
    `o 22 r 6(9)(b) deals with the attached amount`

-- src:3476 | (9) A non‑party who is served with a notice of attachment — ( a )
-- src:3477 | must, within 14 days after service of the notice of attachment, inform the Sheriff of the amount owing by the non‑party to the enforcement respondent that is available to be attached; and
@ref O 22 r 6(9)(a) (src:3476-3477)
`o 22 r 6(9)(a) the duty of the non-party to inform the Sheriff` MEANS
    PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment`
    MUST `o 22 r 6(9)(a) informs the Sheriff of the amount owing to the enforcement respondent that is available to be attached`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST BREACH BY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` BECAUSE "the non-party did not inform the Sheriff of the amount owing within 14 days after service of the notice of attachment"

#TRACE `o 22 r 6(9)(a) the duty of the non-party to inform the Sheriff` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` DOES `o 22 r 6(9)(a) informs the Sheriff of the amount owing to the enforcement respondent that is available to be attached` AT 14

#TRACE `o 22 r 6(9)(a) the duty of the non-party to inform the Sheriff` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` DOES `o 22 r 6(9)(a) informs the Sheriff of the amount owing to the enforcement respondent that is available to be attached` AT 15

-- No act at all: the clock reaches day 15 and the duty to inform is breached by expiry (the deadline is inclusive).
#TRACE `o 22 r 6(9)(a) the duty of the non-party to inform the Sheriff` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

`o 22 r 6(9)(b)(ii) the period before which the non-party must not deal with the attached amount` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 21
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- (9)(b): "must not deal with the attached amount" -- an "until" bar (ruled 2026-11-05 (d)), written as its own
-- yes/no function: JUST TRUE while the bar stands, JUST FALSE after.  The function never says that the non-party
-- has dealt, or may deal, with the amount.
-- src:3478 | ( b )
-- src:3479 | must not deal with the attached amount — (i)
-- src:3480 | if a notice of objection is filed under Rule 10 — until after the notice of objection has been determined in the manner set out in that Rule; or
-- src:3481 | (ii)
-- src:3482 | in any other case — until after 21 days have passed after the date of service of the notice of attachment.
@ref O 22 r 6(9)(b) (src:3478-3482)
GIVEN `a notice of objection is filed under Rule 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of objection has been determined in the manner set out in Rule 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 6(9)(b) the non-party cannot yet deal with the attached amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a notice of objection is filed under Rule 10` AND (NOT `the notice of objection has been determined in the manner set out in Rule 10`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a notice of objection is filed under Rule 10`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a notice of objection is filed under Rule 10 — until after the notice of objection has been determined in the manner set out in that Rule" [until bar: delegated-definitions ruling (d) of 2026-11-05]
        IF `the day asked about` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other case — until after 21 days have passed after the date of service of the notice of attachment" [until bar: delegated-definitions ruling (d) of 2026-11-05]

-- The 21-day bar of (9)(b)(ii) as a regulative rule, for a trace to examine (Meng's note on ruling (d) of 2026-11-05, which is
-- a request about how the bar is modelled and not part of the ruling): the non-party SHANT deal with the attached amount
-- WITHIN the 21 days after service.  An act inside the window is a breach; the window passing without the act is
-- fulfilment, and the last day of the window is inclusive.  Only (9)(b)(ii) is a clock: (9)(b)(i) waits for an event
-- (the determination of the objection) and is the yes/no function above.
-- src:3478 | ( b )
-- src:3479 | must not deal with the attached amount — (i)
-- src:3480 | if a notice of objection is filed under Rule 10 — until after the notice of objection has been determined in the manner set out in that Rule; or
-- src:3481 | (ii)
-- src:3482 | in any other case — until after 21 days have passed after the date of service of the notice of attachment.
@ref O 22 r 6(9)(b)(ii) (src:3478-3482)
`o 22 r 6(9)(b)(ii) the bar on the non-party dealing with the attached amount` MEANS
    PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment`
    SHANT `o 22 r 6(9)(b) deals with the attached amount`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` BECAUSE "the non-party dealt with the attached amount within 21 days after service of the notice of attachment"

-- The window has passed (day 22): the bar is over.
#TRACE `o 22 r 6(9)(b)(ii) the bar on the non-party dealing with the attached amount` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 22)

-- An act inside the window (day 5): breach.
#TRACE `o 22 r 6(9)(b)(ii) the bar on the non-party dealing with the attached amount` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` DOES `o 22 r 6(9)(b) deals with the attached amount` AT 5

-- The last day of the window (day 21) is still inside it: the bar stands.
#TRACE `o 22 r 6(9)(b)(ii) the bar on the non-party dealing with the attached amount` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 21)

`o 22 r 6(10) the period for handing or paying over` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 7
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- (10): "If no notice of objection is filed under Rule 10, the non-party must hand or pay over ... within 7 days after
-- the expiry of the time mentioned in paragraph (9)(b)(ii)".
-- src:3483 | (10) If no notice of objection is filed under Rule 10, the non‑party must hand or pay over — ( a )
-- src:3484 | to the enforcement applicant the money due to the enforcement respondent; and
-- src:3485 | ( b )
-- src:3486 | to the Sheriff the commission due to the Sheriff,
-- src:3487 | within 7 days after the expiry of the time mentioned in paragraph (9)( b )(ii).
@ref O 22 r 6(10) (src:3483-3487)
GIVEN `a notice of objection is filed under Rule 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the non-party hands or pays over the money to the enforcement applicant and the commission to the Sheriff` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 6(10) the non-party hands or pays over in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a notice of objection is filed under Rule 10`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no notice of objection is filed under Rule 10, the non‑party must hand or pay over" [if, marginal reading (a)]
        IF `the date the non-party hands or pays over the money to the enforcement applicant and the commission to the Sheriff` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 7 days after the expiry of the time mentioned in paragraph (9)( b )(ii)" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: day 0 of the trace is the expiry of the 21 days; both payments are due in 7 days.
-- src:3483 | (10) If no notice of objection is filed under Rule 10, the non‑party must hand or pay over — ( a )
-- src:3484 | to the enforcement applicant the money due to the enforcement respondent; and
-- src:3485 | ( b )
-- src:3486 | to the Sheriff the commission due to the Sheriff,
-- src:3487 | within 7 days after the expiry of the time mentioned in paragraph (9)( b )(ii).
@ref O 22 r 6(10) (src:3483-3487)
`o 22 r 6(10) the duty of the non-party to hand or pay over` MEANS
    (PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment`
     MUST `o 22 r 6(10)(a) hands or pays over to the enforcement applicant the money due to the enforcement respondent`
     WITHIN 7
     LEST BREACH BY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` BECAUSE "the money due to the enforcement respondent was not handed or paid over to the enforcement applicant within 7 days after the expiry of the time mentioned in paragraph (9)(b)(ii)")
    RAND
    (PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment`
     MUST `o 22 r 6(10)(b) hands or pays over to the Sheriff the commission due to the Sheriff`
     WITHIN 7
     LEST BREACH BY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` BECAUSE "the commission due to the Sheriff was not handed or paid over within 7 days after the expiry of the time mentioned in paragraph (9)(b)(ii)")

#TRACE `o 22 r 6(10) the duty of the non-party to hand or pay over` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` DOES `o 22 r 6(10)(a) hands or pays over to the enforcement applicant the money due to the enforcement respondent` AT 7
    PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` DOES `o 22 r 6(10)(b) hands or pays over to the Sheriff the commission due to the Sheriff` AT 7

#TRACE `o 22 r 6(10) the duty of the non-party to hand or pay over` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` DOES `o 22 r 6(10)(a) hands or pays over to the enforcement applicant the money due to the enforcement respondent` AT 7
    PARTY `o 22 r 6 the non-party served with the notice of attachment` DOES `o 22 r 6(10)(b) hands or pays over to the Sheriff the commission due to the Sheriff` AT 8

-- No act at all: the clock reaches day 8 and the duty to hand or pay over is breached by expiry.
#TRACE `o 22 r 6(10) the duty of the non-party to hand or pay over` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8)

