-- (1): "after 14 days after a copy of the notice of seizure has been served on the enforcement respondent under
-- Rule 6, unless the movable property is perishable, in which case the Sheriff may take steps to sell the property
-- earlier".  The last day of the 14 days is the O 3 r 3 count.
-- src:3490 | 7. —(1) The Sheriff may take steps to sell seized movable property after 14 days after a copy of the notice of seizure has been served on the enforcement respondent under Rule 6, unless the movable property is perishable, in which case the Sheriff may take steps to sell the property earlier. (2) The Sheriff may take steps to sell seized immovable property after 30 days after the notice of seizure has been served on the enforcement respondent under Rule 6.
@ref O 22 r 7(1) (src:3490-3490)
