GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 22 r 9(3) the Sheriff's commission where the property is not sold` MEANS
    IF `the property is seized or ordered to be sold` AND `the property is not sold for any reason`
    THEN JUST (max `o 22 r 9(2) the least commission` (min `o 22 r 9(2) the greatest commission` (`o 22 r 9(2) the rate of the Sheriff's commission` TIMES (min `the estimated value of the seized property` `the amount stated in the enforcement order to be due to the enforcement applicant`))))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If property is seized or ordered to be sold but not sold for any reason"

-- src:3512 | (3) If property is seized or ordered to be sold but not sold for any reason, the Sheriff is entitled to a commission of 2% of the estimated value of the seized property or the amount stated in the enforcement order to be due to the enforcement applicant (whichever is less), subject to a minimum amount of $100 and a maximum amount of $50,000.
@ref O 22 r 9(3) (src:3512-3512)
GIVEN `the property is seized or ordered to be sold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is not sold for any reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 9(3) the Sheriff is entitled to a commission where the property is not sold` MEANS
    IF `the property is seized or ordered to be sold` AND `the property is not sold for any reason`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If property is seized or ordered to be sold but not sold for any reason"

DECLARE `o 22 r 9(4) item` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 9(4)(a) the gross proceeds of sale of the seized properties`
    `o 22 r 9(4)(b) the enforcement costs`
    `o 22 r 9(4)(c) the amount of money claimed by a landlord, not exceeding 6 months' rent, under section 20 of the Distress Act`
    `o 22 r 9(4)(d) the amount of money available to pay the enforcement applicant`
    `o 22 r 9(4)(e) the amount of money claimed in each enforcement order, in the order of the priority according to the dates of issue`
    `o 22 r 9(4)(f) the amount of money available to return to the enforcement respondent`

-- (4): "the Sheriff must prepare a statement of accounts showing" (a) to (f); (e) only "where there are more than one
-- enforcement order against the same enforcement respondent".
-- src:3513 | (4) Subject to any written law, the Sheriff must prepare a statement of accounts showing — ( a )
-- src:3514 | the gross proceeds of sale of the seized properties;
-- src:3515 | ( b )
-- src:3516 | the enforcement costs;
-- src:3517 | ( c )
-- src:3518 | the amount of money claimed by a landlord, not exceeding 6 months’ rent, under section 20 of the Distress Act;
-- src:3519 | ( d )
-- src:3520 | the amount of money available to pay the enforcement applicant;
-- src:3521 | ( e )
-- src:3522 | where there are more than one enforcement order against the same enforcement respondent, the amount of money claimed in each enforcement order, in the order of the priority according to the dates of issue of the enforcement orders; and
-- src:3523 | ( f )
-- src:3524 | after using the proceeds of sale in sub‑paragraph ( a ) to pay for the items in sub‑paragraphs ( b ) to ( e ), the amount of money available to return to the enforcement respondent.
@ref O 22 r 9(4) (src:3513-3524)
GIVEN item IS A `o 22 r 9(4) item`
      `there is more than one enforcement order against the same enforcement respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 9(4) the statement of accounts must show the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `o 22 r 9(4)(e) the amount of money claimed in each enforcement order, in the order of the priority according to the dates of issue` THEN
        IF `there is more than one enforcement order against the same enforcement respondent`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where there are more than one enforcement order against the same enforcement respondent" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4)(c): the landlord's claim is shown "not exceeding 6 months' rent".
-- src:3517 | ( c )
-- src:3518 | the amount of money claimed by a landlord, not exceeding 6 months’ rent, under section 20 of the Distress Act;
@ref O 22 r 9(4)(c) (src:3517-3518)
GIVEN `the amount of money claimed by the landlord under section 20 of the Distress Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the monthly rent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 22 r 9(4)(c) the amount of the landlord's claim to be shown` MEANS
    min `the amount of money claimed by the landlord under section 20 of the Distress Act` (6 TIMES `the monthly rent`)

-- (5): "The priority of payments is in the order set out in paragraph (4)": the position of an item that is paid
-- from the proceeds, (b) first.  Items (a) and (f) are not payments out of the proceeds.
-- src:3525 | (5) The priority of payments is in the order set out in paragraph (4).
@ref O 22 r 9(5) (src:3525-3525)
GIVEN item IS A `o 22 r 9(4) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 22 r 9(5) the position of the item in the order of priority of payments` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `o 22 r 9(4)(b) the enforcement costs` THEN JUST 1
    WHEN `o 22 r 9(4)(c) the amount of money claimed by a landlord, not exceeding 6 months' rent, under section 20 of the Distress Act` THEN JUST 2
    WHEN `o 22 r 9(4)(d) the amount of money available to pay the enforcement applicant` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `o 22 r 9(4)(e) the amount of money claimed in each enforcement order, in the order of the priority according to the dates of issue` THEN JUST 4
    WHEN `o 22 r 9(4)(a) the gross proceeds of sale of the seized properties` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sub-paragraph (a) is the fund that pays "the items in sub‑paragraphs ( b ) to ( e )", not an item paid from it
    WHEN `o 22 r 9(4)(f) the amount of money available to return to the enforcement respondent` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sub-paragraph (f) is what is left "after using the proceeds of sale in sub‑paragraph ( a ) to pay for the items in sub‑paragraphs ( b ) to ( e )"

-- src:3526 | (6) If the proceeds of sale are not sufficient to pay the enforcement costs, the enforcement applicant must pay the amount of the shortfall to the Sheriff.
@ref O 22 r 9(6) (src:3526-3526)
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale` IS A NUMBER
      `the enforcement costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 9(6) the enforcement applicant must pay the amount of the shortfall to the Sheriff` MEANS
    IF `the proceeds of sale` LESS THAN `the enforcement costs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the proceeds of sale are not sufficient to pay the enforcement costs, the enforcement applicant must pay the amount of the shortfall to the Sheriff" [if, marginal reading (a)]

-- src:3526 | (6) If the proceeds of sale are not sufficient to pay the enforcement costs, the enforcement applicant must pay the amount of the shortfall to the Sheriff.
@ref O 22 r 9(6) (src:3526-3526)
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale` IS A NUMBER
      `the enforcement costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 22 r 9(6) the amount of the shortfall` MEANS
    IF `the proceeds of sale` LESS THAN `the enforcement costs`
    THEN JUST (`the enforcement costs` MINUS `the proceeds of sale`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a number cannot carry the no): the yes/no twin `o 22 r 9(6) the enforcement applicant must pay the amount of the shortfall to the Sheriff` answers JUST FALSE where the proceeds are sufficient

